<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="flavonol biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-3101" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: The expected taxonomic range of the pathway includes Oryza sativa Japonica Group, and, enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Oryza sativa Japonica Group. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; This pathway describes the formation of |FRAME: Flavonols flavonols| with 4&apos;-hydroxylation (|FRAME:CPD1F-90|), 4&apos;,5&apos;-hydroxylation (|FRAME:CPD-520|) and 3&apos;,4&apos;,5&apos;-hydroxylation pattern (|FRAME:MYRICETIN|) from their dihydroflavonol precursors |FRAME:DIHYDROKAEMPFEROL-CMPD|, |FRAME:CPD-474| and |FRAME:CPD-7087|, respectively. The oxidation of the C2-C3 bond of the C ring of the dehydroflavonols to form the corresponding flavonols is carried out by |FRAME:2-KETOGLUTARATE|-dependent dioxygenases (flavonol synthases) |CITS:[22563787][12126705]|. Cytochrome P450-dependent monooxygenases |CITS:[10476065]| provide further interconnectivity and the 3&apos;-hydroxylation of |FRAME:CPD1F-90| to yield |FRAME:CPD-520|, which has been demonstrated in mutants of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;Nicotiana tobaccum&lt;/i&gt; lacking flavonoid 3&apos;monooxygenase activities |CITS:[ 20357139]|, adds another connection to the existing metabolic grid. Certain enzymes, e.g. the flavonol synthases from &lt;i&gt;Citrus unshiu&lt;/i&gt; (CuFLS) |CITS:[12180990] [12620339]| and from the gymnosperm &lt;i&gt;Ginkgo biloba&lt;/i&gt; (GbFLS1) |CITS:[21643949]| are bifunctional and can also act as flavanone 3&amp;beta;-hydroxylase in the |FRAME:PWY1F-FLAVSYN| pathway, hence accommodating more than one pathway. Moreover, the recombinantly expressed and characterized anthocyanidin synthase from &lt;i&gt;Ginkgo biloba&lt;/i&gt; has also been shown to have bifunctional properties by catalyzing the conversion of |FRAME:CPD-474| to form |FRAME:CPD-520|, hence performing a second catalytic activity as flavonol synthase |CITS:[18779661]|. In |FRAME:TAX-3701|, |FRAME:CPD-520| is the primary |FRAME: Flavonols flavonol| in the seeds, and |FRAME:CPD1F-90| is the main |FRAME:Flavonols flavonol| in whole flowers |CITS: [9112784]|. |FRAME:MYRICETIN Myricetin|, which is a widespread flavonol in the plant kingdom, has not been detected in |FRAME:TAX-3701| yet.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="O-28" />
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
    <Author name="hartmut" />
  </Authors>
